{"type":"npc","name":"Terrordactyl","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":80,"temp":0,"max":80,"details":""},"ac":{"value":24,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":40}],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":6},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Terrordactyls are unusual cousins to pterosaurs, with shark-like hammerheads and tough black hides that absorb light and make them difficult to see in shadowy places. Their sturdy, toothy beaks are well-adapted to crushing hard-shelled prey, whether it be insects or armored travelers.</p><p>Terrordactyls roost upside down in caves or on rocky cliffs, where they prepare to ambush potential prey passing below. Against large groups, they often prefer to swoop down and take a bite out of each creature, testing which is tastiest. Once they pick their favorite morsel, a terrordactyl tears it apart with their sharp talons.</p><p>Due to their voracious appetites, terrordactyls are often solitary hunters that zealously guard their favored territories. They bury their eggs in concealed rocky crevices, often in caves or cliff faces. Terrordactyls who are nesting or who are raising young are particularly fierce, as they remove any potential threats to their offspring and gather additional prey to feed them.</p><h2>Territories of Terror</h2><p>In addition to natural rocky features, terrordactyls occasionally make their homes in abandoned ruins. These frightening creatures have been responsible for more than one tale of unearthly screaming emanating from an abandoned castle. For such arrangements to persist long-term, however, the ruin needs to provide sufficient food. When wandering wildlife fails to suffice, adventurers coming to investigate rumors of hauntings might provide supplemental nutrition. In time, the victims of terrordactyl attacks might just make those rumors about lingering ghosts a reality.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 30/65/125 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing), armor (medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> air, bane, charisma, darkness, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality), sensory (low-light vision), wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Kelsey Dionne","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":3},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":1},"int":{"mod":-4},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":14,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"},{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":15,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":12,"special":[{"label":"to Grab","predicate":["action:grapple"],"base":15}]},"intimidation":{"base":14,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":13,"special":[{"label":"in dim light or darkness","predicate":[{"or":["lighting:dim-light","lighting:darkness"]}],"base":15}]},"survival":{"base":12,"special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["animal"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"_id":"LDWiSl3QVxJjuisU","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/terrordactyl.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Terrordactyl","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":2,"height":2,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/terrordactyl.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"r